    <desc>Reopen the windows, tabs and panes of the last session, and remember the window size.</desc>
  </info>

  <title>Restore your windows and tabs</title>

<p>When <app>Pano Terminal</app> is started without arguments while none of
  its windows are open, for example from the applications menu, it reopens
  the windows, tabs and panes that were open when it was last closed. Each
  terminal gets a new shell in its previous folder, with its profile and
  its title. Programs that were running are not restored.</p>

  <p>To turn this off:</p>
  <steps>
<item><p>Press the menu button in the top-right corner of the window and select <gui style="menuitem">Preferences</gui>.</p></item>
<item><p>In the <gui>Behavior</gui> group, turn off <gui>Restore Session</gui>.</p></item>
</steps>

  <p>The session is kept in the folder <file>~/.local/state/pano-terminal</file>.</p>

  <section id="window-size">
    <title>Remember the window size</title>

    <p>New windows normally get the initial size of their profile, see
    <link xref="app-terminal-sizes"/>. To open them with the size of the
    terminal you used last instead:</p>
    <steps>
<item><p>Press the menu button in the top-right corner of the window and select <gui style="menuitem">Preferences</gui>.</p></item>
<item><p>In the <gui>Behavior</gui> group, turn on <gui>Remember Window Size</gui>.</p></item>
</steps>
  </section>

